# Everything in this repo is consumed by Linux: deploy.sh runs under bash,
# the Python and the Dockerfile run in a container, and Terraform compares
# its heredocs byte-for-byte against what AWS stored.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows checks out CRLF and three things break
# at once: bash fails on deploy.sh with "$'\r': command not found",
# Terraform reports a permanent phantom diff on the CodeBuild buildspec,
# and the image build ships \r into the container. Normalising here means
# it cannot depend on whose machine did the clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.pt binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
